---@field secretManagerConfig? gcp.container_v1.SecretManagerConfig Secret CSI driver configuration.
---@field fleet? gcp.container_v1.Fleet Fleet information for the cluster.
---@field workloadIdentityConfig? gcp.container_v1.WorkloadIdentityConfig Configuration for the use of Kubernetes Service Accounts in IAM policies.
---@field currentNodeVersion? string Output only. Deprecated, use [NodePools.version](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/reference/rest/v1/projects.locations.clusters.nodePools) instead. The current version of the node software components. If they are currently at multiple versions because they're in the process of being upgraded, this reflects the minimum version of all nodes.
---@field currentMasterVersion? string Output only. The current software version of the master endpoint.
---@field selfLink? string Output only. Server-defined URL for the resource.
---@field subnetwork? string The name of the Google Compute Engine [subnetwork](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/subnetworks) to which the cluster is connected.
---@field controlPlaneEndpointsConfig? gcp.container_v1.ControlPlaneEndpointsConfig Configuration for all cluster's control plane endpoints.
---@field maintenancePolicy? gcp.container_v1.MaintenancePolicy Configure the maintenance policy for this cluster.
---@field currentEmulatedVersion? string Output only. The current emulated version of the master endpoint. The version is in minor version format, e.g. 1.30. No value or empty string means the cluster has no emulated version.
---@field nodePools? gcp.container_v1.NodePoolList The node pools associated with this cluster. This field should not be set if "node_config" or "initial_node_count" are specified.
---@field nodeIpv4CidrSize? number Output only. The size of the address space on each node for hosting containers. This is provisioned from within the `container_ipv4_cidr` range. This field will only be set when cluster is in route-based network mode.
---@field confidentialNodes? gcp.container_v1.ConfidentialNodes Configuration of Confidential Nodes. All the nodes in the cluster will be Confidential VM once enabled.
---@field scheduleUpgradeConfig? gcp.container_v1.ScheduleUpgradeConfig Optional. Configuration for scheduled upgrades.
---@field securityPostureConfig? gcp.container_v1.SecurityPostureConfig Optional. Enable/Disable Security Posture API features for the cluster.
---@field description? string An optional description of this cluster.
---@field binaryAuthorization? gcp.container_v1.BinaryAuthorization Configuration for Binary Authorization.
---@field labelFingerprint? string The fingerprint of the set of labels for this cluster.
---@field enableKubernetesAlpha? boolean Kubernetes alpha features are enabled on this cluster. This includes alpha API groups (e.g. v1alpha1) and features that may not be production ready in the kubernetes version of the master and nodes. The cluster has no SLA for uptime and master/node upgrades are disabled. Alpha enabled clusters are automatically deleted thirty days after creation.
---@field meshCertificates? gcp.container_v1.MeshCertificates Configuration for issuance of mTLS keys and certificates to Kubernetes pods.
---@field managedOpentelemetryConfig? gcp.container_v1.ManagedOpenTelemetryConfig Configuration for Managed OpenTelemetry pipeline.
---@field defaultMaxPodsConstraint? gcp.container_v1.MaxPodsConstraint The default constraint on the maximum number of pods that can be run simultaneously on a node in the node pool of this cluster. Only honored if cluster created with IP Alias support.
---@field shieldedNodes? gcp.container_v1.ShieldedNodes Shielded Nodes configuration.
---@field name? string The name of this cluster. The name must be unique within this project and location (e.g. zone or region), and can be up to 40 characters with the following restrictions: * Lowercase letters, numbers, and hyphens only. * Must start with a letter. * Must end with a number or a letter.
---@field podAutoscaling? gcp.container_v1.PodAutoscaling The config for pod autoscaling.
---@field networkPolicy? gcp.container_v1.NetworkPolicy Configuration options for the NetworkPolicy feature.
---@field nodeCreationConfig? gcp.container_v1.NodeCreationConfig Optional. Configuration for Node Creation Mode.
---@field tpuIpv4CidrBlock? string Output only. The IP address range of the Cloud TPUs in this cluster, in [CIDR](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classless_Inter-Domain_Routing) notation (e.g. `1.2.3.4/29`). This field is deprecated due to the deprecation of 2VM TPU. The end of life date for 2VM TPU is 2025-04-25.
---@field secretSyncConfig? gcp.container_v1.SecretSyncConfig Configuration for sync Secret Manager secrets as k8s secrets.
---@field locations? gcp.container_v1.StringList The list of Google Compute Engine [zones](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available) in which the cluster's nodes should be located. This field provides a default value if [NodePool.Locations](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/reference/rest/v1/projects.locations.clusters.nodePools#NodePool.FIELDS.locations) are not specified during node pool creation. Warning: changing cluster locations will update the [NodePool.Locations](https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/reference/rest/v1/projects.locations.clusters.nodePools#NodePool.FIELDS.locations) of all node pools and will result in nodes being added and/or removed.
---@field instanceGroupUrls? gcp.container_v1.StringList Output only. Deprecated. Use node_pools.instance_group_urls.
---@field masterAuthorizedNetworksConfig? gcp.container_v1.MasterAuthorizedNetworksConfig The configuration options for master authorized networks feature. Deprecated: Use ControlPlaneEndpointsConfig.IPEndpointsConfig.authorized_networks_config instead.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The time the cluster was created, in [RFC3339](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt) text format.
---@field initialClusterVersion? string The initial Kubernetes version for this cluster. Valid versions are those found in validMasterVersions returned by getServerConfig. The version can be upgraded over time; such upgrades are reflected in currentMasterVersion and currentNodeVersion. Users may specify either explicit versions offered by Kubernetes Engine or version aliases, which have the following behavior: - "latest": picks the highest valid Kubernetes version - "1.X": picks the highest valid patch+gke.N patch in the 1.X version - "1.X.Y": picks the highest valid gke.N patch in the 1.X.Y version - "1.X.Y-gke.N": picks an explicit Kubernetes version - "","-": picks the default Kubernetes version
---@field gkeAutoUpgradeConfig? gcp.container_v1.GkeAutoUpgradeConfig Configuration for GKE auto upgrades.
---@field enableK8sBetaApis? gcp.container_v1.K8sBetaAPIConfig Beta APIs Config
---@field currentNodeCount? number Output only. The number of nodes currently in the cluster. Deprecated. Call Kubernetes API directly to retrieve node information.
---@field initialNodeCount? number The number of nodes to create in this cluster. You must ensure that your Compute Engine [resource quota](https://cloud.google.com/compute/quotas) is sufficient for this number of instances. You must also have available firewall and routes quota. For requests, this field should only be used in lieu of a "node_pool" object, since this configuration (along with the "node_config") will be used to create a "NodePool" object with an auto-generated name. Do not use this and a node_pool at the same time. This field is deprecated, use node_pool.initial_node_count instead.
---@field releaseChannel? gcp.container_v1.ReleaseChannel Release channel configuration. If left unspecified on cluster creation and a version is specified, the cluster is enrolled in the most mature release channel where the version is available (first checking STABLE, then REGULAR, and finally RAPID). Otherwise, if no release channel configuration and no version is specified, the cluster is enrolled in the REGULAR channel with its default version.
---@field monitoringConfig? gcp.container_v1.MonitoringConfig Monitoring configuration for the cluster.
---@field resourceUsageExportConfig? gcp.container_v1.ResourceUsageExportConfig Configuration for exporting resource usages. Resource usage export is disabled when this config is unspecified.
---@field endpoint? string Output only. The IP address of this cluster's master endpoint. The endpoint can be accessed from the internet at `https://username:password@endpoint/`. See the `masterAuth` property of this resource for username and password information.
---@field statusMessage? string Output only. Deprecated. Use conditions instead. Additional information about the current status of this cluster, if available.
---@field enterpriseConfig? gcp.container_v1.EnterpriseConfig GKE Enterprise Configuration. Deprecated: GKE Enterprise features are now available without an Enterprise tier.
---@field managedMachineLearningDiagnosticsConfig? gcp.container_v1.ManagedMachineLearningDiagnosticsConfig Configuration for Managed Machine Learning Diagnostics.
---@field authenticatorGroupsConfig? gcp.container_v1.AuthenticatorGroupsConfig Configuration controlling RBAC group membership information.
---@field network? string The name of the Google Compute Engine [network](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/networks-and-firewalls#networks) to which the cluster is connected. If left unspecified, the `default` network will be used.
---@field clusterIpv4Cidr? string The IP address range of the container pods in this cluster, in [CIDR](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classless_Inter-Domain_Routing) notation (e.g. `10.96.0.0/14`). Leave blank to have one automatically chosen or specify a `/14` block in `10.0.0.0/8`.
---@field databaseEncryption? gcp.container_v1.DatabaseEncryption Configuration of etcd encryption.
---@field location? string Output only. The name of the Google Compute Engine [zone](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/regions-zones/regions-zones#available) or [region](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/regions-zones/regions-zones#available) in which the cluster resides.
---@field loggingService? string The logging service the cluster should use to write logs. Currently available options: * `logging.googleapis.com/kubernetes` - The Cloud Logging service with a Kubernetes-native resource model * `logging.googleapis.com` - The legacy Cloud Logging service (no longer available as of GKE 1.15). * `none` - no logs will be exported from the cluster. If left as an empty string,`logging.googleapis.com/kubernetes` will be used for GKE 1.14+ or `logging.googleapis.com` for earlier versions.
---@field rbacBindingConfig? gcp.container_v1.RBACBindingConfig RBACBindingConfig allows user to restrict ClusterRoleBindings an RoleBindings that can be created.
---@field privateClusterConfig? gcp.container_v1.PrivateClusterConfig Configuration for private cluster.
---@field legacyAbac? gcp.container_v1.LegacyAbac Configuration for the legacy ABAC authorization mode.
---@field costManagementConfig? gcp.container_v1.CostManagementConfig Configuration for the fine-grained cost allocation feature.
---@field enableTpu? boolean Enable the ability to use Cloud TPUs in this cluster. This field is deprecated due to the deprecation of 2VM TPU. The end of life date for 2VM TPU is 2025-04-25.
---@field autopilot? gcp.container_v1.Autopilot Autopilot configuration for the cluster.
---@field id? string Output only. Unique id for the cluster.
---@field zone? string Output only. The name of the Google Compute Engine [zone](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available) in which the cluster resides. This field is deprecated, use location instead.
---@field satisfiesPzs? boolean Output only. Reserved for future use.
---@field servicesIpv4Cidr? string Output only. The IP address range of the Kubernetes services in this cluster, in [CIDR](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classless_Inter-Domain_Routing) notation (e.g. `1.2.3.4/29`). Service addresses are typically put in the last `/16` from the container CIDR.
---@field etag? string This checksum is computed by the server based on the value of cluster fields, and may be sent on update requests to ensure the client has an up-to-date value before proceeding.
---@field expireTime? string Output only. The time the cluster will be automatically deleted in [RFC3339](https://www.ietf.org/rfc/rfc3339.txt) text format.
---@field status? gcp.container_v1.ClusterStatusEnum|string Output only. The current status of this cluster.
---@field notificationConfig? gcp.container_v1.NotificationConfig Notification configuration of the cluster.
---@field nodePoolAutoConfig? gcp.container_v1.NodePoolAutoConfig Node pool configs that apply to all auto-provisioned node pools in autopilot clusters and node auto-provisioning enabled clusters.
---@field masterAuth? gcp.container_v1.MasterAuth The authentication information for accessing the master endpoint. If unspecified, the defaults are used: For clusters before v1.12, if master_auth is unspecified, `username` will be set to "admin", a random password will be generated, and a client certificate will be issued.
---@field conditions? gcp.container_v1.StatusConditionList Which conditions caused the current cluster state.
---@field networkConfig? gcp.container_v1.NetworkConfig Configuration for cluster networking.
---@field identityServiceConfig? gcp.container_v1.IdentityServiceConfig Configuration for Identity Service component.
---@field compliancePostureConfig? gcp.container_v1.CompliancePostureConfig Optional. Deprecated: Compliance Posture is no longer supported. For more details, see https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/deprecations/posture-management-deprecation. Enable/Disable Compliance Posture features for the cluster.
---@field autoscaling? gcp.container_v1.ClusterAutoscaling Cluster-level autoscaling configuration.
---@field anonymousAuthenticationConfig? gcp.container_v1.AnonymousAuthenticationConfig Configuration for limiting anonymous access to all endpoints except the health checks.
---@field parentProductConfig? gcp.container_v1.ParentProductConfig The configuration of the parent product of the cluster. This field is used by Google internal products that are built on top of the GKE cluster and take the ownership of the cluster.
---@field nodeConfig? gcp.container_v1.NodeConfig Parameters used in creating the cluster's nodes. For requests, this field should only be used in lieu of a "node_pool" object, since this configuration (along with the "initial_node_count") will be used to create a "NodePool" object with an auto-generated name. Do not use this and a node_pool at the same time. For responses, this field will be populated with the node configuration of the first node pool. (For configuration of each node pool, see `node_pool.config`) If unspecified, the defaults are used. This field is deprecated, use node_pool.config instead.
---@field addonsConfig? gcp.container_v1.AddonsConfig Configurations for the various addons available to run in the cluster.
---@field rollbackSafeUpgrade? gcp.container_v1.RollbackSafeUpgrade Optional. The rollback safe upgrade information of the cluster. This field is used when user manually triggers a rollback safe upgrade.

---ClusterAutoscaling contains global, per-cluster information required by Cluster Autoscaler to automatically adjust the size of the cluster and create/delete node pools based on the current needs.
---@class gcp.container_v1.ClusterAutoscaling
---@field autoscalingProfile? gcp.container_v1.ClusterAutoscalingAutoscalingProfileEnum|string Defines autoscaling behaviour.
---@field autoprovisioningNodePoolDefaults? gcp.container_v1.AutoprovisioningNodePoolDefaults AutoprovisioningNodePoolDefaults contains defaults for a node pool created by NAP.
---@field autopilotGeneralProfile? gcp.container_v1.ClusterAutoscalingAutopilotGeneralProfileEnum|string Autopilot general profile for the cluster, which defines the configuration for the cluster.
---@field defaultComputeClassConfig? gcp.container_v1.DefaultComputeClassConfig Default compute class is a configuration for default compute class.
---@field resourceLimits? gcp.container_v1.ResourceLimitList Contains global constraints regarding minimum and maximum amount of resources in the cluster.
---@field enableNodeAutoprovisioning? boolean Enables automatic node pool creation and deletion.
---@field autoprovisioningRestrictionConfig? gcp.container_v1.AutoprovisioningRestrictionConfig Optional. Configures restrictions related to autoprovisioning settings.
---@field autoprovisioningLocations? gcp.container_v1.StringList The list of Google Compute Engine [zones](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available) in which the NodePool's nodes can be created by NAP.

---@alias gcp.container_v1.ClusterAutoscalingAutopilotGeneralProfileEnum "AUTOPILOT_GENERAL_PROFILE_UNSPECIFIED"|"NO_PERFORMANCE"|"NONE"

---@alias gcp.container_v1.ClusterAutoscalingAutoscalingProfileEnum "PROFILE_UNSPECIFIED"|"OPTIMIZE_UTILIZATION"|"BALANCED"

---@alias gcp.container_v1.ClusterList gcp.container_v1.Cluster[]

---Configuration of network bandwidth tiers
---@class gcp.container_v1.ClusterNetworkPerformanceConfig
---@field totalEgressBandwidthTier? gcp.container_v1.ClusterNetworkPerformanceConfigTotalEgressBandwidthTierEnum|string Specifies the total network bandwidth tier for NodePools in the cluster.

---@alias gcp.container_v1.ClusterNetworkPerformanceConfigTotalEgressBandwidthTierEnum "TIER_UNSPECIFIED"|"TIER_1"

---ClusterPolicyConfig stores the configuration for cluster wide policies.
---@class gcp.container_v1.ClusterPolicyConfig
---@field noSystemMutation? boolean Denotes that preventing creation and mutation of resources in GKE managed namespaces and cluster-scoped GKE managed resources .
---@field noUnsafeWebhooks? boolean Denotes preventing unsafe webhooks.
---@field noStandardNodePools? boolean Denotes preventing standard node pools and requiring only autopilot node pools.
---@field noSystemImpersonation? boolean Denotes preventing impersonation and CSRs for GKE System users.

---@alias gcp.container_v1.ClusterStatusEnum "STATUS_UNSPECIFIED"|"PROVISIONING"|"RUNNING"|"RECONCILING"|"STOPPING"|"ERROR"|"DEGRADED"

---ClusterUpdate describes an update to the cluster. Exactly one update can be applied to a cluster with each request, so at most one field can be provided.
---@class gcp.container_v1.ClusterUpdate
---@field desiredNodePoolAutoConfigLinuxNodeConfig? gcp.container_v1.LinuxNodeConfig The desired Linux node config for all auto-provisioned node pools in autopilot clusters and node auto-provisioning enabled clusters. Currently only `cgroup_mode` can be set here.
---@field desiredPrivateIpv6GoogleAccess? gcp.container_v1.ClusterUpdateDesiredPrivateIpv6GoogleAccessEnum|string The desired state of IPv6 connectivity to Google Services.
---@field desiredDatabaseEncryption? gcp.container_v1.DatabaseEncryption Configuration of etcd encryption.
---@field desiredEnableMultiNetworking? boolean Enable/Disable Multi-Networking for the cluster
---@field desiredNotificationConfig? gcp.container_v1.NotificationConfig The desired notification configuration.
---@field desiredNodePoolAutoscaling? gcp.container_v1.NodePoolAutoscaling Autoscaler configuration for the node pool specified in desired_node_pool_id. If there is only one pool in the cluster and desired_node_pool_id is not provided then the change applies to that single node pool.
---@field desiredFleet? gcp.container_v1.Fleet The desired fleet configuration for the cluster.
---@field desiredPrivilegedAdmissionConfig? gcp.container_v1.PrivilegedAdmissionConfig The desired privileged admission config for the cluster.
---@field desiredCompliancePostureConfig? gcp.container_v1.CompliancePostureConfig Deprecated: Compliance Posture is no longer supported. For more details, see https://cloud.google.com/kubernetes-engine/docs/deprecations/posture-management-deprecation. Enable/Disable Compliance Posture features for the cluster.
---@field desiredSecurityPostureConfig? gcp.container_v1.SecurityPostureConfig Enable/Disable Security Posture API features for the cluster.
---@field desiredNodeVersion? string The Kubernetes version to change the nodes to (typically an upgrade). Users may specify either explicit versions offered by Kubernetes Engine or version aliases, which have the following behavior: - "latest": picks the highest valid Kubernetes version - "1.X": picks the highest valid patch+gke.N patch in the 1.X version - "1.X.Y": picks the highest valid gke.N patch in the 1.X.Y version - "1.X.Y-gke.N": picks an explicit Kubernetes version - "-": picks the Kubernetes master version
---@field desiredPrivateClusterConfig? gcp.container_v1.PrivateClusterConfig The desired private cluster configuration. master_global_access_config is the only field that can be changed via this field. See also ClusterUpdate.desired_enable_private_endpoint for modifying other fields within PrivateClusterConfig. Deprecated: Use desired_control_plane_endpoints_config.ip_endpoints_config.global_access instead.
---@field desiredEnterpriseConfig? gcp.container_v1.DesiredEnterpriseConfig The desired enterprise configuration for the cluster. Deprecated: GKE Enterprise features are now available without an Enterprise tier.
---@field desiredManagedMachineLearningDiagnosticsConfig? gcp.container_v1.ManagedMachineLearningDiagnosticsConfig The desired managed machine learning diagnostics configuration.
---@field desiredControlPlaneEndpointsConfig? gcp.container_v1.ControlPlaneEndpointsConfig Control plane endpoints configuration.
---@field desiredMonitoringConfig? gcp.container_v1.MonitoringConfig The desired monitoring configuration.
---@field desiredNodePoolId? string The node pool to be upgraded. This field is mandatory if "desired_node_version", "desired_image_family" or "desired_node_pool_autoscaling" is specified and there is more than one node pool on the cluster.
---@field userManagedKeysConfig? gcp.container_v1.UserManagedKeysConfig The Custom keys configuration for the cluster. This field is deprecated. Use ClusterUpdate.desired_user_managed_keys_config instead.
---@field desiredBinaryAuthorization? gcp.container_v1.BinaryAuthorization The desired configuration options for the Binary Authorization feature.
---@field desiredClusterAutoscaling? gcp.container_v1.ClusterAutoscaling Cluster-level autoscaling configuration.
---@field desiredNodePoolAutoConfigKubeletConfig? gcp.container_v1.NodeKubeletConfig The desired node kubelet config for all auto-provisioned node pools in autopilot clusters and node auto-provisioning enabled clusters.
---@field desiredManagedOpentelemetryConfig? gcp.container_v1.ManagedOpenTelemetryConfig The desired managed open telemetry configuration.
---@field enableK8sBetaApis? gcp.container_v1.K8sBetaAPIConfig Kubernetes open source beta apis enabled on the cluster. Only beta apis
---@field desiredAddonsConfig? gcp.container_v1.AddonsConfig Configurations for the various addons available to run in the cluster.
---@field desiredMasterAuthorizedNetworksConfig? gcp.container_v1.MasterAuthorizedNetworksConfig The desired configuration options for master authorized networks feature. Deprecated: Use desired_control_plane_endpoints_config.ip_endpoints_config.authorized_networks_config instead.
---@field desiredResourceUsageExportConfig? gcp.container_v1.ResourceUsageExportConfig The desired configuration for exporting resource usage.
---@field gkeAutoUpgradeConfig? gcp.container_v1.GkeAutoUpgradeConfig Configuration for GKE auto upgrade.
---@field desiredEnablePrivateEndpoint? boolean Enable/Disable private endpoint for the cluster's master. Deprecated: Use desired_control_plane_endpoints_config.ip_endpoints_config.enable_public_endpoint instead. Note that the value of enable_public_endpoint is reversed: if enable_private_endpoint is false, then enable_public_endpoint will be true.
---@field desiredNodeKubeletConfig? gcp.container_v1.NodeKubeletConfig The desired node kubelet config for the cluster.
---@field etag? string The current etag of the cluster. If an etag is provided and does not match the current etag of the cluster, update will be blocked and an ABORTED error will be returned.
---@field desiredRbacBindingConfig? gcp.container_v1.RBACBindingConfig RBACBindingConfig allows user to restrict ClusterRoleBindings an RoleBindings that can be created.
---@field desiredImage? string The desired name of the image to use for this node. This is used to create clusters using a custom image. NOTE: Set the "desired_node_pool" field as well.
---@field desiredAutopilotWorkloadPolicyConfig? gcp.container_v1.WorkloadPolicyConfig WorkloadPolicyConfig is the configuration related to GCW workload policy
---@field desiredAutopilotClusterPolicyConfig? gcp.container_v1.ClusterPolicyConfig The desired autopilot cluster policies that to be enforced in the cluster.
---@field desiredDisableL4LbFirewallReconciliation? boolean Enable/Disable L4 LB VPC firewall reconciliation for the cluster.
---@field desiredDefaultEnablePrivateNodes? boolean Override the default setting of whether future created nodes have private IP addresses only, namely NetworkConfig.default_enable_private_nodes
---@field desiredImageType? string The desired image type for the node pool. NOTE: Set the "desired_node_pool" field as well.
---@field desiredMasterVersion? string The Kubernetes version to change the master to. Users may specify either explicit versions offered by Kubernetes Engine or version aliases, which have the following behavior: - "latest": picks the highest valid Kubernetes version - "1.X": picks the highest valid patch+gke.N patch in the 1.X version - "1.X.Y": picks the highest valid gke.N patch in the 1.X.Y version - "1.X.Y-gke.N": picks an explicit Kubernetes version - "-": picks the default Kubernetes version
---@field desiredShieldedNodes? gcp.container_v1.ShieldedNodes Configuration for Shielded Nodes.
---@field desiredLoggingConfig? gcp.container_v1.LoggingConfig The desired logging configuration.
---@field desiredEmulatedVersion? string Optional. The desired emulated version for the cluster.
---@field desiredUserManagedKeysConfig? gcp.container_v1.UserManagedKeysConfig The desired user managed keys config for the cluster.
---@field desiredGatewayApiConfig? gcp.container_v1.GatewayAPIConfig The desired config of Gateway API on this cluster.
---@field desiredMeshCertificates? gcp.container_v1.MeshCertificates Configuration for issuance of mTLS keys and certificates to Kubernetes pods.
---@field desiredVerticalPodAutoscaling? gcp.container_v1.VerticalPodAutoscaling Cluster-level Vertical Pod Autoscaling configuration.
---@field desiredDnsConfig? gcp.container_v1.DNSConfig DNSConfig contains clusterDNS config for this cluster.
---@field desiredPodAutoscaling? gcp.container_v1.PodAutoscaling The desired config for pod autoscaling.
---@field desiredAnonymousAuthenticationConfig? gcp.container_v1.AnonymousAuthenticationConfig Configuration for limiting anonymous access to all endpoints except the health checks.
---@field removedAdditionalPodRangesConfig? gcp.container_v1.AdditionalPodRangesConfig The additional pod ranges that are to be removed from the cluster. The pod ranges specified here must have been specified earlier in the 'additional_pod_ranges_config' argument.
---@field desiredNodePoolLoggingConfig? gcp.container_v1.NodePoolLoggingConfig The desired node pool logging configuration defaults for the cluster.
---@field desiredEnableCiliumClusterwideNetworkPolicy? boolean Enable/Disable Cilium Clusterwide Network Policy for the cluster.
---@field desiredDatapathProvider? gcp.container_v1.ClusterUpdateDesiredDatapathProviderEnum|string The desired datapath provider for the cluster.
---@field desiredLocations? gcp.container_v1.StringList The desired list of Google Compute Engine [zones](https://cloud.google.com/compute/docs/zones#available) in which the cluster's nodes should be located. This list must always include the cluster's primary zone. Warning: changing cluster locations will update the locations of all node pools and will result in nodes being added and/or removed.
---@field desiredSecretManagerConfig? gcp.container_v1.SecretManagerConfig Enable/Disable Secret Manager Config.
---@field desiredAmbientNetworkingConfig? gcp.container_v1.AmbientNetworkingConfig Optional. The desired ambient networking configuration.
---@field desiredAdditionalIpRangesConfig? gcp.container_v1.DesiredAdditionalIPRangesConfig The desired config for additional subnetworks attached to the cluster.
---@field desiredParentProductConfig? gcp.container_v1.ParentProductConfig The desired parent product config for the cluster.
---@field desiredImageProject? string The project containing the desired image to use for this node. This is used to create clusters using a custom image. NOTE: Set the "desired_node_pool" field as well.
---@field desiredEnableFqdnNetworkPolicy? boolean Enable/Disable FQDN Network Policy for the cluster.
---@field desiredContainerdConfig? gcp.container_v1.ContainerdConfig The desired containerd config for the cluster.
---@field desiredInTransitEncryptionConfig? gcp.container_v1.ClusterUpdateDesiredInTransitEncryptionConfigEnum|string Specify the details of in-transit encryption.
---@field desiredNodePoolAutoConfigNetworkTags? gcp.container_v1.NetworkTags The desired network tags that apply to all auto-provisioned node pools in autopilot clusters and node auto-provisioning enabled clusters.
---@field desiredIdentityServiceConfig? gcp.container_v1.IdentityServiceConfig The desired Identity Service component configuration.
---@field desiredMonitoringService? string The monitoring service the cluster should use to write metrics. Currently available options: * `monitoring.googleapis.com/kubernetes` - The Cloud Monitoring service with a Kubernetes-native resource model * `monitoring.googleapis.com` - The legacy Cloud Monitoring service (no longer available as of GKE 1.15). * `none` - No metrics will be exported from the cluster. If left as an empty string,`monitoring.googleapis.com/kubernetes` will be used for GKE 1.14+ or `monitoring.googleapis.com` for earlier versions.
---@field desiredControlPlaneEgress? gcp.container_v1.ControlPlaneEgress The desired control plane egress control config for the cluster.
---@field desiredNetworkTierConfig? gcp.container_v1.NetworkTierConfig The desired network tier configuration for the cluster.
---@field desiredSecretSyncConfig? gcp.container_v1.SecretSyncConfig Configuration for sync Secret Manager secrets as k8s secrets.
---@field desiredNetworkPerformanceConfig? gcp.container_v1.ClusterNetworkPerformanceConfig The desired network performance config.
---@field desiredGcfsConfig? gcp.container_v1.GcfsConfig The desired GCFS config for the cluster
---@field desiredAutoIpamConfig? gcp.container_v1.AutoIpamConfig AutoIpamConfig contains all information related to Auto IPAM
---@field desiredAuthenticatorGroupsConfig? gcp.container_v1.AuthenticatorGroupsConfig The desired authenticator groups config for the cluster.
---@field desiredL4ilbSubsettingConfig? gcp.container_v1.ILBSubsettingConfig The desired L4 Internal Load Balancer Subsetting configuration.
---@field desiredNodeCreationConfig? gcp.container_v1.NodeCreationConfig Optional. The desired NodeCreationConfig for the cluster.
---@field desiredDefaultSnatStatus? gcp.container_v1.DefaultSnatStatus The desired status of whether to disable default sNAT for this cluster.
---@field desiredReleaseChannel? gcp.container_v1.ReleaseChannel The desired release channel configuration.
---@field desiredK8sBetaApis? gcp.container_v1.K8sBetaAPIConfig Desired Beta APIs to be enabled for cluster.
---@field desiredStackType? gcp.container_v1.ClusterUpdateDesiredStackTypeEnum|string The desired stack type of the cluster. If a stack type is provided and does not match the current stack type of the cluster, update will attempt to change the stack type to the new type.
