---The `Status` type defines a logical error model that is suitable for different programming environments, including REST APIs and RPC APIs. It is used by [gRPC](https://github.com/grpc). Each `Status` message contains three pieces of data: error code, error message, and error details. You can find out more about this error model and how to work with it in the [API Design Guide](https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/errors).
---@class gcp.container_v1.Status
---@field code? number The status code, which should be an enum value of google.rpc.Code.
---@field message? string A developer-facing error message, which should be in English. Any user-facing error message should be localized and sent in the google.rpc.Status.details field, or localized by the client.
---@field details? gcp.container_v1.DocumentMapList A list of messages that carry the error details. There is a common set of message types for APIs to use.

---StatusCondition describes why a cluster or a node pool has a certain status (e.g., ERROR or DEGRADED).
---@class gcp.container_v1.StatusCondition
---@field code? gcp.container_v1.StatusConditionCodeEnum|string Machine-friendly representation of the condition Deprecated. Use canonical_code instead.
---@field message? string Human-friendly representation of the condition
---@field canonicalCode? gcp.container_v1.StatusConditionCanonicalCodeEnum|string Canonical code of the condition.

---@alias gcp.container_v1.StatusConditionCanonicalCodeEnum "OK"|"CANCELLED"|"UNKNOWN"|"INVALID_ARGUMENT"|"DEADLINE_EXCEEDED"|"NOT_FOUND"|"ALREADY_EXISTS"|"PERMISSION_DENIED"|"UNAUTHENTICATED"|"RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED"|"FAILED_PRECONDITION"|"ABORTED"|"OUT_OF_RANGE"|"UNIMPLEMENTED"|"INTERNAL"|"UNAVAILABLE"|"DATA_LOSS"

---@alias gcp.container_v1.StatusConditionCodeEnum "UNKNOWN"|"GCE_STOCKOUT"|"GKE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_DELETED"|"GCE_QUOTA_EXCEEDED"|"SET_BY_OPERATOR"|"CLOUD_KMS_KEY_ERROR"|"CA_EXPIRING"|"NODE_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_MISSING_PERMISSIONS"|"CLOUD_KMS_KEY_DESTROYED"

---@alias gcp.container_v1.StatusConditionList gcp.container_v1.StatusCondition[]

